academic_requirements:
DEGREE REQUIREMENT: a Bachelor's degree, university diploma or equivalent foreign qualification of at least three years' duration.

CURRICULAR REQUIREMENTS (Programme Regulations, Art. 2, issued with Rectoral Decree no. 786 of 28 July 2025, applicable to cohorts from a.y. 2025/2026):
(a) holders of a Bachelor's degree in Industrial Engineering, class L-9 (ex DM 270/04 or DM 1648/23), awarded by the University of Trento automatically satisfy the curricular requirements;
(b) holders of a class L-9 Industrial Engineering degree from ANOTHER Italian university must have earned at least 12 ECTS in the characterising Management Engineering scientific-disciplinary sectors of Table A: IIND-04/A Tecnologie e sistemi di lavorazione (ex ING-IND/16), IIND-05/A Impianti industriali meccanici (ex ING-IND/17), IEGE-01/A Ingegneria economico-gestionale (ex ING-IND/35), IINF-04/A Automatica (ex ING-INF/04);
(c) holders of an Italian degree in a class OTHER than L-9 must satisfy Table B, whose minimum ECTS are: 24 ECTS in the mathematics/statistics group (MATH-02/A Algebra, MATH-02/B Geometria, MATH-03/A Analisi matematica, MATH-03/B Probabilita e statistica matematica, MATH-04/A Fisica matematica, MATH-05/A Analisi numerica, STAT-01/A Statistica, STAT-01/B Statistica per la ricerca sperimentale e tecnologica, STAT-04/A Metodi matematici dell'economia); 15 ECTS in the physics/chemistry group (PHYS-03/A, PHYS-06/A, CHEM-03/A, CHEM-05/A, CHEM-06/A); and 36 ECTS across a broad industrial/information engineering group (IIND-04/A, IIND-05/A, IEGE-01/A, IINF-04/A, IIND-01/F Fluidodinamica, IIND-02/A Meccanica applicata alle macchine, IIND-03/A Progettazione meccanica, IIND-03/B Disegno e metodi dell'ingegneria industriale, IIND-03/C Metallurgia, IIND-06/A Macchine a fluido, IIND-06/B Sistemi per l'energia e l'ambiente, IIND-07/A Fisica tecnica industriale, IIND-07/B Fisica tecnica ambientale, IMIS-01/A, IMIS-01/B, IMAT-01/A Scienze e tecnologie dei materiali, ICHI-01/A, IIET-01/A Elettrotecnica, IIND-08/A, IBIO-01/A Bioingegneria, IINF-01/A Elettronica, IINF-02/A, IINF-03/A Telecomunicazioni, IINF-05/A, CEAR-01/A Idraulica, CEAR-06/A Scienza delle costruzioni, ECON-07/A Economia e gestione delle imprese);
(d) holders of a foreign qualification, or of a qualification from a system without ECTS, have their curricular requirements assessed by a Committee appointed by the Departmental Council, on the basis of equivalences between the content of previously passed courses and the disciplinary sectors of Table B.

MINIMUM GRADE / PERSONAL PREPARATION: enrolment with academic debts is NOT allowed. Candidates under (b), (c) and (d) who lack part of the curricular ECTS must acquire the missing credits BEFORE the assessment of personal preparation - they can do so by enrolling in 'Single Courses for Master's Degrees' and passing the corresponding exams by the registration deadline. Personal preparation is considered adequate if the weighted average mark of the exams passed in the first-cycle degree, EXCLUDING the final examination, is at least 23/30 (a mark of '30 cum laude' counts as 31/30). For applicants with a foreign qualification, the weighted average is assessed as the GPA in the grading system of the country of graduation, and the assessment of personal preparation may additionally include a test/interview before the Committee appointed by the Departmental Council.

NON-EU QUOTA AND SELECTION SCORE (2026/2027 call): 25 seats reserved for non-European citizens resident abroad (including the places assigned within the EIT Manufacturing programme). The Bachelor's degree must be obtained by 30 June 2026 for non-Europeans graduating outside Italy (31 October 2026 for Europeans and equivalents and for non-Europeans graduating in Italy with a valid study permit). Applications are scored out of 100: up to 30 points for coherence between previous studies and the objectives of the Master's degree; up to 60 points for the curriculum studiorum (marks and results in previous studies, post-graduate courses, extra-academic activities); up to 10 points for additional language skills (English above B2 or other languages). Candidates scoring 50/100 or above are eligible; ties are resolved in favour of the youngest candidate. Candidates scoring at least 70/100 at the top of the list may be awarded a scholarship. Applicants may apply to more than one DII master, but must submit (and pay for) a separate application for each.

EU/EQUIVALENTS ROUTE: candidates may apply even before graduating and before completing all exams; the outcome of the evaluation is communicated by email by the Student Support Service (for a.y. 2025/2026 the stated turnaround was 'within one month of application submission').
